doc:sch-1-sec-92e a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "92E Period for which authorisations remain in force" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "An authorisation under this Division is in force for the period:  (a) starting on the day specified in the determination (which may be before the commencement of this section, but must not be before 1 April 2026); and  (b) ending at the earliest of the following:  (i) the start of the day specified in the determination;  (ii) if the determination is revoked—the end of the day the revocation takes effect;  (iii) the end of the last day on which a declaration mentioned in subsection 92D(2) to which the determination relates is in force." ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-92f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "92F Variation of authorisations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-92f ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may, at any time, make a determination in writing to vary an authorisation under this Division if the Commission considers it appropriate to do so.  Exceptional circumstances exemption powers  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 48, 2026 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Responding to Exceptional Circumstances) Act 2026  (2) The Commission must not make a determination under subsection (1) varying an authorisation unless the Commission is satisfied that, in all the circumstances, the conduct specified in the authorisation as varied would assist, or would be likely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or emergency to which the declaration relates.  (3) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:  (a) must have regard to:  (i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the assistance, or likely assistance, in response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances to which the declaration relates; and  (ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely to result, from the conduct; and  (b) may have regard to any other public benefit that would result or likely result from the conduct.  (4) The Commission must give the person who applied for the authorisation written notice stating:  (a) that the authorisation is varied; and  (b) details of the variation; and  (c) the date on which the variation takes effect.  (5) The variation takes effect on the business day after the day on which the notice is given." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may, at any time, make a determination in writing to vary an authorisation under this Division if the Commission considers it appropriate to do so.  Exceptional circumstances exemption powers  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 48, 2026 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Responding to Exceptional Circumstances) Act 2026  (2) The Commission must not make a determination under subsection (1) varying an authorisation unless the Commission is satisfied that, in all the circumstances, the conduct specified in the authorisation as varied would assist, or would be likely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or emergency to which the declaration relates.  (3) In making a determination under subsection (1), the Commission:  (a) must have regard to:  (i) the likely benefit to the public resulting from the assistance, or likely assistance, in response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances to which the declaration relates; and  (ii) the detriment to the public that would result, or be likely to result, from the conduct; and  (b) may have regard to any other public benefit that would result or likely result from the conduct.  (4) The Commission must give the person who applied for the authorisation written notice stating:  (a) that the authorisation is varied; and  (b) details of the variation; and  (c) the date on which the variation takes effect.  (5) The variation takes effect on the business day after the day on which the notice is given."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a9573a09187bd5b5c1b002b825139987ca2fbdf06a99312d1c2c44686e6f1bf5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-92f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-92f-ss-2 ;
