concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-95ad a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "95AD Commission may withdraw the benefit of exceptional"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-95ad ;
    values:originalText "circumstances class exemptions in particular case  (1) The Commission may give a person a written notice if:  (a) a determination in force under section 95AC specifies a kind of conduct; and  (b) the Commission considers that:  (i) conduct of that kind would not assist, or would not be likely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or emergency specified in the determination; or  (ii) conduct of that kind is not appropriate.  Exceptional circumstances exemption powers  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 48, 2026 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Responding to Exceptional Circumstances) Act 2026  (2) The Commission must, in or with the notice under subsection (1), give the person a written statement of its reasons for giving the notice.  (3) While a notice under subsection (1) is in force, the determination does not apply to the conduct specified in the notice engaged in by the person.  (4) The notice under subsection (1):  (a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person the notice; and  (b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:  (i) if the Commission revokes the notice—the day after the day the Commission gives the person the written notice;  (ii) the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to be in force." ;
    skos:definition "circumstances class exemptions in particular case  (1) The Commission may give a person a written notice if:  (a) a determination in force under section 95AC specifies a kind of conduct; and  (b) the Commission considers that:  (i) conduct of that kind would not assist, or would not be likely to assist, in the response to or recovery from the exceptional circumstances or emergency specified in the determination; or  (ii) conduct of that kind is not appropriate.  Exceptional circumstances exemption powers  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 48, 2026 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Responding to Exceptional Circumstances) Act 2026  (2) The Commission must, in or with the notice under subsection (1), give the person a written statement of its reasons for giving the notice.  (3) While a notice under subsection (1) is in force, the determination does not apply to the conduct specified in the notice engaged in by the person.  (4) The notice under subsection (1):  (a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person the notice; and  (b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:  (i) if the Commission revokes the notice—the day after the day the Commission gives the person the written notice;  (ii) the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to be in force."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8610110535410b7d0859e29ed394fb87453ab771154740d773dffa2830977e27" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-95ad-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-95ad-ss-2 ;
