concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-95ad-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "95AD(4) Commission may withdraw the benefit of exceptional"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-95ad-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The notice under subsection (1):  (a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person the notice; and  (b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:  (i) if the Commission revokes the notice—the day after the day the Commission gives the person the written notice;  (ii) the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to be in force." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The notice under subsection (1):  (a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person the notice; and  (b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:  (i) if the Commission revokes the notice—the day after the day the Commission gives the person the written notice;  (ii) the time the determination under section 95AC ceases to be in force."@en ;
