doc:sch-1-sec-95af-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "95AF(1) Extension of declaration of exceptional circumstances" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, extend the operation of a declaration under section 95AE if the Minister is satisfied that the exceptional circumstances mentioned in subparagraph 95AE(1)(a)(i) are likely to continue to exist beyond the period in which the order will be in force." ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-responding-to-exceptional-circumstances-act-2026-sch-1-sec-95af-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "95AF(2) Extension of declaration of exceptional circumstances"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-95af-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Minister may, under subsection (1), extend the operation of an order more than once. However, each period of extension must not exceed 3 months.  Exceptional circumstances exemption powers  Schedule 1 Consequential amendments  Part 2  No. 48, 2026 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Responding to Exceptional Circumstances) Act 2026" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The Minister may, under subsection (1), extend the operation of an order more than once. However, each period of extension must not exceed 3 months.  Exceptional circumstances exemption powers  Schedule 1 Consequential amendments  Part 2  No. 48, 2026 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Responding to Exceptional Circumstances) Act 2026"@en ;
